    {
      "title": "Stephen Miller, Trump’s incoming chief of staff, pledges ‘total devotion’ to the president",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/07/stephen-miller-trump-loyalty",
      "description": "<p>Hardline aide offers ‘unwavering commitment’ to president amid fears White House will double down on far-right immigration agenda</p><p>Stephen Miller, <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump\">Donald Trump</a>’s most controversial aide and the architect of his sweeping immigration crackdown, has lavished praise on the president after his appointment as White House chief of staff.</p><p>In his first public remarks since the move was announced, Miller – who begins the role on Monday – pledged “total devotion” to Trump amid concern the administration is now poised to double down on its far-right, nativist immigration agenda.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/07/stephen-miller-trump-loyalty\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-07T15:15:11"
    },
    {
      "title": "Trump’s elevation of Stephen Miller a middle finger to millions of voters",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/07/trump-stephen-miller-midterms",
      "description": "<p>Architect of Trump’s far-right immigration agenda is now most powerful unelected figure in government – it suggests White House is moving to a war footing</p><p>Donald Trump just gave the middle finger to millions of American voters.</p><p>Any other president who suffered the kind of drubbing at the polls that Trump did this week might have felt at least a sliver of humility – and perhaps even an<strong> </strong>obligation to work with the new opposition in Congress.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/07/trump-stephen-miller-midterms\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-07T13:00:12"
    },
